        <h1>LeetCode 2472: Maximum Number of Non-overlapping Palindrome Substrings (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a string s and a positive integer k. Select a set of non-overlapping substrings
                from s such that each substring has a length of at least k and each substring is a palindrome.
                Return the maximum number of substrings in such a set. A substring is a contiguous sequence of
                characters within a string.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "abaccdbbd", k = 3<br>
                Output: 2<br>
                Explanation: The substrings "aba" and "dbbd" are both palindromes of length at least 3 and do
                not overlap, so the answer is 2.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int maxPalindromes(string s, int k) {
        int n = s.size();
        if (k == 1) return n;

        int count = 0;

        for (int pos = 0; pos &lt;= n - k;) {
            int jump = 1;

            for (int len : {k, k + 1}) {
                if (pos + len &lt;= n &amp;&amp;
                    equal(s.begin() + pos,
                          s.begin() + pos + (len &gt;&gt; 1),
                          s.rbegin() + (n - (pos + len)))) {
                    jump = len;
                    count++;
                    break;
                }
            }

            pos += jump;
        }

        return count;
    }
};</code></pre>
